  "party_positions": [
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "MOAC Mall Holdings LLC",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "808b7a2483191fac3e3f79e0be5b48fff808def10cdfc55a6781b101b100d24b",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-808b7a248319-0000-0006"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 9,
                "start": 9
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to MOAC Mall Holdings LLC, mOAC contends that the sale of the property under \u00a7363(b) had already closed, the money was paid to Sears, and the transaction is not subject to adjustment even if the designated leases are later found ineligible for assignment."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "MR. HALLWARD-DRIEMEIER",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "808b7a2483191fac3e3f79e0be5b48fff808def10cdfc55a6781b101b100d24b",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-808b7a248319-0001-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 24,
                "start": 24
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to MR. HALLWARD-DRIEMEIER, mOAC suggests that additional relief could be provided to Mall of America from the compensation of the sale."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "MR. HALLWARD-DRIEMEIER",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "808b7a2483191fac3e3f79e0be5b48fff808def10cdfc55a6781b101b100d24b",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-808b7a248319-0001-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 25,
                "start": 25
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to MR. HALLWARD-DRIEMEIER, mOAC argues that the rule only precludes invalidation of the sale; because the transaction is an assignment, not a sale, the rule does not apply."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "MOAC Mall Holdings LLC",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Transform",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "6ee6e08cf4391831e6dec252e0ed2eedfc3afa07c1debfc5b045b4e9f98e3a74",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-6ee6e08cf439-0001-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 15,
                "start": 15
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Transform argues that \u00a7363(b) sales of estate assets must proceed under a court\u2019s in\u2011rem jurisdiction, which requires the court to have actual or constructive control over the res (including leaseholds)."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Transform Holdco LLC",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "808b7a2483191fac3e3f79e0be5b48fff808def10cdfc55a6781b101b100d24b",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-808b7a248319-0000-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 5,
                "start": 5
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Transform Holdco LLC, transform maintains that the requirement of a stay is not jurisdictional; therefore it is subject to waiver, forfeiture, and estoppel, which apply here."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Transform Holdco LLC",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Ms. Sinzdak",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "808b7a2483191fac3e3f79e0be5b48fff808def10cdfc55a6781b101b100d24b",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-808b7a248319-0001-0004"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 27,
                "start": 27
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Ms. Sinzdak, the United States, as amicus, argues that \u00a7363(m) is not jurisdictional because its text does not suggest jurisdictional effect and there is no clear\u2011statement evidence that it is jurisdictional."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "United States (Amicus Curiae)",
